  "description": "Noteblock Pianola — an interactive 3D music box that plays MIDI through a Minecraft-themed soundfont.",
  "type": "module",
  "scripts": {
    "dev": "bunx serve . -l 8080",
    "build": "bun build ./src/musicbox/main.js --outdir ./dist --minify --sourcemap=linked",
    "sync": "node tools/sync.js",
    "sync:full": "node tools/sync.js --full"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "three": "0.169.0"
  }
}
</file>

<file path="README.md">
A fun noteblock player piano! 

Custom model animation made using blockbench, rendered with threejs. All sound is handled with spessasynth and a modified instrument transposed sf2 file.

Midis sourced from:
- https://pianola.co.nz/public/
- https://musescore.com/
- https://bitmidi.com/
- https://www.zaxpax.com/disney1.htm
- https://torbid.tljhome.com/midi/disney.html
- https://www.midis101.com/
- https://www.midi-karaoke.info/
- https://pianorollmusic.org/

A few in my library are sourced from the following, but I don't think any are contained in this repo:
- http://www.pianorollmusic.org/rolldatabase.php
- https://github.com/pianoroll/SUPRA
- https://www.kunstderfuge.com/piano-rolls.htm


## Dependencies

- [spessasynth_lib](https://github.com/spessasus/spessasynth_lib)  
  Used for audio synthesis. Licensed under Apache 2.0.

- [three.js](https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js)  
  Used for 3D rendering. Licensed under MIT.
</file>

